{# Comments, via giscus: the thread is a GitHub Discussion in the site repo,
   so there is no backend here and nothing to moderate but the Discussion
   itself. Rendered only once site.json carries the real ids, so a build made
   before they are pasted in simply has no comment section rather than a
   broken widget. A post can opt out with `comments: false` in its front
   matter.

   The widget is injected by /assets/comments.js rather than by a script tag
   here, because its theme has to be read from the page at load time and kept
   in step with the colour toggle afterwards. #}
{% if site.comments and "REPLACE" not in site.comments.repoId and comments != false %}
<section class="comments">
  <hr class="rule">
  <h2>Comments</h2>
  <p class="commentnote">Signed in with GitHub. Threads live in
    <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.comments.repo }}/discussions">the repo's discussions</a>.</p>
  <div id="comments"
       data-repo="{{ site.comments.repo }}"
       data-repo-id="{{ site.comments.repoId }}"
       data-category="{{ site.comments.category }}"
       data-category-id="{{ site.comments.categoryId }}"
       data-theme-dark="{{ site.comments.themeDark }}"
       data-theme-light="{{ site.comments.themeLight }}"></div>
</section>
{% endif %}
